  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.3.0: More fixes found by the regression suite; a test that relied on the wrong result can start to fail. Date pickers (flatpickr, Bootstrap 3) work on machines with non-English regional settings: day, month and AM/PM are looked up in English and HaveValue formats the expected date with the invariant culture (before, e.g. \"Oktober 5, 2026\" or \"05.10.2026\"). The flatpickr day and AM/PM are clicked with VAF's click, which scrolls and retries when they are covered. LetsSelectOptionFromRightClickMenu waits for the browser's menu before the key presses. AsSlideBar().Should().HaveValue() works (the assertion class was internal and HaveValue threw NotImplementedException). 3.2.0: Fixes found by the new regression suite; a test that relied on the wrong result can start to fail. HaveAlert() waits for the alert (ElementWaitTimeout) instead of taking it at once. AsPane().Should().HaveValue() compares the text, as LetsGetValue() returns it, not the Name attribute. IsVisible() is false for a hidden element. LetsCheckIfWindowExists() stays on the current window, and a LetsSwitchToWindow / LetsSwitchToWindowByURL that finds nothing goes back to it. New: AsSection() on an element found with HaveElement. 3.1.1: Fix: Should().NotHaveElement<T>() on a section passed even when the element was visible; it now fails then, so a test that relied on the wrong result can start to fail. 3.1.0: Chrome also starts when the test runs as administrator (e.g. Visual Studio run as admin); before, Chrome relaunched itself without admin rights and the driver failed with \"Chrome instance exited\". New: BrowserOptions.ConfigureChrome and ConfigureFirefox, and the ChromeArguments / FirefoxArguments settings (VAF_ChromeArguments), add browser options while Testing.On<Chrome>() stays as it is. 3.0.0: .NET 10 alongside .NET Framework 4.7.2, with the same API. No test framework dependency: failed checks throw VafAssertionException, which NUnit 3 and 4, MSTest and xUnit report as a failed test. Only Selenium as a dependency. Settings from VAF_* environment variables or app.config. New: Testing.On(browser) for a browser created with settings (remote grid, extra arguments); LetsSaveScreenshotTo; AndAlso() also after a check; HTML report named per test; a .NET 5-9 project stops at build with error VAF0001. Removed: BrowserStack, the mobile types, WinFormApplication, InternetExplorer and the MSTest v1 screenshot overload. Upgrading from 2.x: see \"Migrating from 2.x\" in the README.",
